config AMPERE_CRB_FTPM
	bool
	default n
	depends on !CRB_TPM && !AMD_CRB_FTPM
	select TPM_STARTUP_IGNORE_POSTINIT
	help
	  Ampere firmware TPM (fTPM) with Command Response Buffer support.
	  The fTPM runs in the secure world (TF-A, EL3) and is reached by
	  submitting the command to the CRB control area and then making an
	  SMC call to invoke the TPM service handler. The SoC provides the
	  address of the control area and the SMC function ID with
	  ampere_ftpm_get_params().

	  TF-A already sends TPM2_Startup to the fTPM, so the TPM2_Startup
	  coreboot issues returns TPM_RC_INITIALIZE and is ignored.
